 ## Code Standards
+
+### Blender 4.4 API correctness (mandatory)
+
+- Membership in `bpy_prop_collection` is string-based. Use
+  `if obj.name not in collection.objects:`; never write
+  `if obj not in collection.objects:`.
+- Before assigning a shader socket, respect its dimensionality. Color/vector
+  sockets require a tuple (RGBA for colors); scalar sockets require a float.
+  In particular, Blender 4.4 `Sheen Tint` can be a color socket, so do not
+  blindly assign `0.0` based only on the socket name.
+- Prefer the demonstrated Blender API patterns below over invented keyword
+  arguments or compatibility branches.
 
